-the-wise">Yaroslav the Wise</a> becomes sole ruler and defeats the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#pechenegs">Pechenegs</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1097</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#council-of-liubech">Council of Liubech</a> confirms each prince's hereditary patrimony</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1169</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#andrei-bogolyubsky">Andrei Bogolyubsky</a> of Vladimir-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#suzdal">Suzdal</a> sacks <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kyiv">Kiev</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1240</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#batu-khan">Batu Khan</a>'s Mongol army storms and sacks <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kyiv">Kiev</a></span></li></ol>
